          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Riemann zeta function
            is the archetypical example of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function"} zeta function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi s
                  %mo ↦
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi n
                        %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\zeta \colon s \mapsto \underoverset{n = 1}{\infty}{\sum} \frac{1}{n^s}
                  \\,.
          %p
            From the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1"} F1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+functions"} zeta functions
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curves"} arithmetic curves
            given by more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+fields"} number fields
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+zeta+functions"} Dedekind zeta functions
            – and over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+fields"} function fields
            – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+zeta+function"} Weil zeta function
            – and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curves"} complex curves
            – the Selberg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+of+a+Riemann+surface"} zeta function of a Riemann surface
            – and in another direction for higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+schemes"} arithmetic schemes
            – the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+zeta+functions"} arithmetic zeta functions
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#special_values Special values
          %p
